  36:     """
  37:     Drop the blue sprites downward relative to the red divider, with vertical sprites passing through to the bottom.
  38: 
  39:     Input structure:
  40:     - The background is the dominant color.
  41:     - One non-background color forms a single full-width horizontal divider row.
  42:     - The other non-background color forms 4-connected sprites above the divider.
  43: 
  44:     Rule:
  45:     - Clear the original sprite pixels.
  46:     - A one-column sprite falls to the bottom of its column and deletes the divider
  47:       pixel it crossed.
  48:     - Any wider sprite falls until its unique widest horizontal row is immediately
  49:       above the divider row; if the moved sprite overlaps the divider, it covers it.
  50: 
  51:     Key insight:
  52:     The red row is not a generic floor: only one-column sprites pass through to the
  53:     bottom, while wider sprites are registered by their widest horizontal segment.
  54:     """
